  "summary": "Skills collection with benign network/CLI helpers",
  "details": "Package ships a collection of 'skills' with assorted helper scripts. Static pattern matches cluster around ordinary network and CLI utilities: a Python scraper and API server using HTTP GET/POST and 'ping' in base_scraper.py and serve_api.py, a benchmark harness referencing curl and 'install' tokens in run-benchmarks.sh, an install.sh for the rclone-cli skill that fetches from the official rclone.org endpoint, and a verify.sh for a youtube-notetaker skill using curl for GET requests. No npm lifecycle hooks (preinstall/install/postinstall) are observed invoking these scripts, no hardcoded attacker-controlled destinations are present, no credential/env-var scraping or home-directory secret enumeration appears, and the only remote host identified (rclone.org) is the official project domain for the tool that skill wraps. The matched patterns reflect bundled developer/skills tooling rather than installer-side attack behavior.",
